<!--
Reference material only — not legal or regulatory advice. See DISCLAIMER.md in the
imda-ai-governance skill. Verify against the official IMDA / AI Verify Foundation publication.

SYSTEM CARD — the "food label" for a generative AI system: one per model-backed
feature or system (a chat assistant, summariser, RAG Q&A bot, or the generative layer
under an agent). Follows the seven disclosure areas of the Model AI Governance
Framework for Generative AI (2024) [MGF-GenAI Trusted Development, p.14].

Written for a team that DEPLOYS a model it may not have trained. "Data used" means the
data YOU added (fine-tuning sets, RAG corpora, few-shot banks) plus what the model
provider discloses about the base model. Where the provider discloses nothing, write
"not disclosed by provider" — don't guess.

PAIRS WITH AGENT_CARD.md: if this system is (part of) an agent, the agent card covers
identity, tools, permissions, approvals and operations and links here; this card covers
the model, its data and its generated content. Don't duplicate content between them.

The framework calibrates disclosure against protecting proprietary information and
expects more for higher-risk systems. Mark each section as INTERNAL or PUBLIC; a
public version may summarise, but the internal version holds the evidence.

SETUP
  1. Copy next to the agent card (agentRegistry folder) or into the feature's docs,
     e.g. docs/systems/<system-id>.md.
  2. Replace every {{PLACEHOLDER}}. Delete guidance comments once filled.
  3. Update on every model, prompt, fine-tune, corpus or filter change that passes
     through checklists/change-review.md. Bump the card version.
-->

